# Full System Audit — Brainstorm Report

**Date:** 2026-06-05
**Scope:** All 3 components (CLI Rust, Cloud Go, Dashboard Next.js)
**Goal:** Review architecture, logic, patterns; fix issues; all tests pass + builds green
**Total LOC:** ~10,400

## Problem Statement

System built rapidly across multiple phases. Need systematic audit to catch logic errors, inconsistent patterns, missing error handling, broken tests, and integration gaps before investor demos.

## Decomposition (6 Sub-projects, Sequential)

| # | Sub-Project | Files | Done Criteria |
|---|------------|-------|---------------|
| 1 | CLI Core | filter, dedup, read_dedup, session, waste, router, events, tracking, security | `cargo test` green, logic verified |
| 2 | CLI Binary | main, hooks, wrap, stats, sync, auth, paths | Commands work, hook contract valid |
| 3 | Cloud API | handlers, middleware, clickhouse client, nats, migrations | `go test ./...` green |
| 4 | Dashboard | pages, api client, hooks, components, auth bypass | `next build` green, all pages 200 |
| 5 | Integration | proto schema Rust↔Go, docker-compose, env vars, CORS | Schema parity, config alignment |
| 6 | CI + Final | Run all suites, verify CI workflows, produce findings | All green |

## Approach Per Sub-project

1. Read every source file
2. Check logic correctness, error handling, edge cases
3. Flag inconsistent or risky patterns
4. Run tests, fix failures
5. Verify build

## Constraints

- Windows host — Go builds blocked by AppControl (Docker required)
- Rust builds work locally via cargo
- Next.js builds work locally via npm
- ClickHouse/NATS only available via Docker

## Decision

Start with Sub-project 1 (CLI Core) immediately. Sequential execution through all 6.
